### Testing (Before Deploy)
- [ ] **Fresh login**: new user logs in, tokens stored in offline sync + localStorage
- [ ] **App reopen (valid token)**: close and reopen app, no redirect, protected routes load
- [ ] **App reopen (expired token)**: close app for >1 hour, reopen, token refreshed silently, no splash loop
- [ ] **Refresh fails (invalid refresh token)**: close app, invalidate refresh token externally, reopen, app redirects to login cleanly (no infinite loop)
- [ ] **Offline after login**: log in, turn off network, close/reopen app, auth state restored from offline sync, app loads (read-only mode if sync disabled)
- [ ] **Network during startup**: start app with no network, wait for timeout, fallback to offline sync, no hang
- [ ] **Multi-tab consistency**: log in on tab A, switch to tab B, B should see updated auth state from sync
- [ ] **Service worker 401 handling**: make an API call that returns 401, verify SW posts message, app redirects to login
- [ ] **iOS PWA specific**: save to home screen, close app fully, reopen, verify no splash screen or redirect loop
- [ ] **Logout**: clear auth state from offline sync + localStorage, verify all protected routes redirect to login

### Security Review
- [ ] Refresh token endpoint requires HTTPS only
- [ ] Refresh token is never logged or exposed in error messages
- [ ] idToken is decoded client-side only (never sent to third-party endpoints)
- [ ] authState in offline sync is marked as uid-scoped (not shared with household)
- [ ] Service worker doesn't cache 401 responses
- [ ] Middleware checks authState before rendering (no client-side-only checks for security)

### Performance & UX
- [ ] Startup validation completes in <500ms (hit cache, no network call needed if token valid)
- [ ] Splash screen/loader shown only during first app launch or refresh; not on every reopen
- [ ] No flash of login screen if already authenticated
- [ ] Offline sync merges auth state without blocking other syncs

### Integration
- [ ] Offline sync module exports a `getAuthState()` function that app can read
- [ ] AuthContext provides single source of truth for `authReady` and `user` state
- [ ] App redirects use the same login href everywhere (no hardcoded paths)
- [ ] Firebase auth config matches across API endpoint and client SDK

